From: picowl <picowl@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] backend/drm: hardware rotation and copy-type connectors

Add wlr_drm_connector_supports_hw_rotation(),
wlr_drm_connector_set_hw_rotation() (primary plane "rotation" property,
90/270 swap the wlr_output_mode size) and wlr_drm_connector_set_copy_type()
(release the scanned-out fb after the page-flip for drivers which copy the
damage to device memory during the commit). Atomic only. A rotated
primary plane refuses buffers whose dst box is not the whole output
(direct scanout falls back to compositing), and a commit enabling a CRTC
whose primary plane cannot do the rotation fails instead of sending the
swapped modes unrotated. The rotation and copy-type state is reset when
the connector's output is destroyed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [picowl specific]
---
